[ti:Take Me Out to the Ball Game]
[ar:Jack Norworth (1908)]
[length:02:35]
[by:SingLearn - Nhom 10 (auto-aligned, faster-whisper)]
[00:13.42]Katie Casey was baseball mad,
[00:17.22]Had the fever and had it bad.
[00:20.44]Just to root for the home town crew,
[00:23.44]Every sou, Katie blew.
[00:27.04]On a Saturday, her young beau
[00:30.00]Called to see if she'd like to go
[00:33.20]To see a show, but Miss Katie said "No,
[00:36.96]Let me tell you what I'd like to know,"
[00:40.52]Take me out to the ball game,
[00:43.42]Take me out with the crowd;
[00:46.74]Buy me some peanuts and Cracker Jack,
[00:49.94]I don't care if I never get back.
[00:52.62]Let me root, root, root for the home team,
[00:56.16]If they don't win, it's a shame.
[00:59.08]For it's one, two, three strikes, you're out,
[01:02.56]At the old ball game.
[02:26.10]
